kernel-spec — Unlicense / public-domain reference trees
========================================================

These directories are **not** GSys LibreCore original work. They are kept as
read-only ancestors for writing the rust-generated ZealOS-shaped BIOS kernel.
Do not relicense. Do not edit copyright, LICENSE, or NOTICE files inside them
(E-UPSTREAMWRITE analog). They are not Cargo members and are not linked.

ZealOS/
  Source: https://github.com/Zeal-Operating-System/ZealOS
  License: Unlicense (public domain dedication)
  Role: primary service-contract ancestor (Adam, DolDoc, ZealC, Gr, Compiler)

TempleOS/
  Source: https://github.com/cia-foundation/TempleOS
  License: public domain (Terry A. Davis / TempleOS)
  Role: original HolyC / Adam / Kernel / Compiler snapshot

goja/
  Source: https://github.com/dop251/goja
  License: MIT (Dmitry Panov / Robert Krimen)
  Role: ES5 VM *semantic* spec; never a Go module or Cargo dependency

lirx-dom/
  Source: https://github.com/lirx-js/dom
  License: MIT (Valentin Richard)
  Role: DOM mutation locality spec; never linked

webidl/
  Source: Mozilla WebIDL (MPL-2.0) via riscv-compilers/libwasm
  Role: interface catalog for the lightweight BIOS browser

svelte-d/
  Source: https://github.com/etcimon/svelte-d
  License: MIT (Etienne Cimon)
  Role: Svelte → libwasm/WASM UI compiler spec; never LDC/Binaryen in this package

botan/
  Source: riscv-dev/botan (Botan, BSD-2-Clause; Jack Lloyd et al. / Etienne Cimon D port)
  Role: TLS 1.2, X.509, RSA, ECDSA reference; never compiled here

libwasm/
  Source: riscv-compilers/libwasm (MIT; Sebastiaan Koppe / Etienne Cimon druntime-wasm)
  Role: WASM-JIT druntime + fetch/Object_Call spec; never compiled here

First-party BIOS code stays MIT under g6lc_bios/crates/**.
Generated ZealC (KMain.ZC, Adam.ZC, …) is MIT, produced by g6b-design from a
BoardSpec — it is a rewrite, not a copy of these trees.
